    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] In July 2013, the campus changed its name to Hansberry College Prep in honor of Lorraine Hansberry, an African-American writer and playwright who grew up on Chicago's south side and who worked to combat racial segregation in the 1950s and 1960s.\n[2] Lorraine Vivian Hansberry (May 19, 1930 – January 12, 1965) was an African-American playwright and writer.\n[3] \"To Be Young, Gifted and Black: Lorraine Hansberry in her Own Words\", was written by Lorraine Hansberry, an American writer best known for her 1957 play \"A Raisin in the Sun\", a play that made Hansberry the first black author of a show on Broadway.\n[4] Sandra Gulland (born November 3, 1944) is an American-born Canadian novelist."
